"Patashu" <Patashu@hotmail.com> writes:
> If I were to complete the game with a conduct outside of those the game
> tracks, what would be an interesting one to try?

I just ascended unihornless, Elberethless and price-ID-less. The latter
two are part of my normal play style. Going unihornless was a one-off,
and actually quite hard -- I hadn't realized just how much I depend on
them for things like potion ID, polyfodder, buffing abused stats and
of course the obvious status fixes...

Artifactless (exception: invocation artifacts) might be another interesting
one. I seem to remember hearing of folks pulling off MR-less, if you want
something harder. Some months ago, I made a joke post about "with one hand
tied behind your back" in regards a conduct where you couldn't use two-
handed weapons or weapon+shield, or do a number of other minor things.

There was a thread a while back about "inventoryless", where you drop
your starting inventory immediately, and from that point on you aren't
allow to pick up anything apart from the Plot Object, the invocation
artifacts and seven candles. Insanely hard and massively
luck-dependent; I came close to getting inventoryless intrinsic
poly-control a couple times before deciding I wasn't sufficiently
masochistic to bother.  Obvious strategies involve pets,
altar-squatting and self-polys.


